From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:43:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Name a command stall at fail-stop

When the oldest command makes no completion-stamp progress until its
deadline, the driver fail-stops with a message that cannot tell a GPU
or firmware that stopped from work that finished but whose receipt the
host never accepted: the progress check watches the oldest command's
stage stamps, and it sees no movement in either case.

Before the fail-stop, print the oldest command's stage targets next to
the stamps the firmware last wrote, the per-stage pending values the
deadline watched, and the number of commands in flight. Only the
fail-stop path prints; nothing else changes.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/recovery.rs | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/recovery.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/recovery.rs
index db1acc5ee1..b255131d47 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/recovery.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/recovery.rs
@@ -254,6 +254,26 @@ pub(crate) fn check_hangs(&mut self, done: &mut Completions) -> Result {
                     self.dev(),
                     "M4 GPU administrative command deadline exceeded without firmware recovery; retaining owners and fail-stop (not proof of quiescence)\n"
                 );
+                // Name the stall: an unreached stamp means the GPU or firmware stopped; every stamp
+                // reached means the work finished and its receipt was never accepted on the host.
+                if let Some(f) = self.engine.oldest() {
+                    let r = &self.graph.render;
+                    let c = &self.graph.compute;
+                    dev_err!(
+                        self.dev(),
+                        "M4 GPU stall: oldest computes {} renders {} target c {:#x} ta {:#x} fs {:#x}; stamps c {:#x} ta {:#x} fs {:#x}; pending {:?}; flights {}\n",
+                        f.computes,
+                        f.renders,
+                        f.target,
+                        f.ta_target,
+                        f.fs_target,
+                        c.fw_stamp.r32(0).unwrap_or(u32::MAX),
+                        r.fw_stamp[0].r32(0).unwrap_or(u32::MAX),
+                        r.fw_stamp[1].r32(0).unwrap_or(u32::MAX),
+                        self.engine.progress,
+                        self.engine.flights.len()
+                    );
+                }
                 self.fail_stop(ETIMEDOUT, done);
                 return Err(ETIMEDOUT);
             }
